{"id": "EUVD-2026-59229", "enisaUuid": "98fc59b4-c3cf-3b2a-b0eb-e31f1b0297e5", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet/tls: Consume empty data records in tls_sw_read_sock()\n\nA peer may send a zero-length TLS application_data record; TLS 1.3\nexplicitly permits these as a traffic-analysis countermeasure (RFC\n8446, Section 5.1). After decryption such a record has full_len ==\n0. tls_sw_read_sock() hands it to the read_actor, which has no\npayload to consume and returns zero. The loop treats a zero return\nas backpressure (used <= 0), requeues the skb at the head of\nrx_list, and stops. rx_list is serviced head-first on the next\ncall, so the empty record is dequeued, fails the same way, and is\nrequeued again; every later record on the connection is blocked\nbehind it.\n\ntls_sw_recvmsg() does not stall on this: a zero-length data record\ncopies nothing and falls through to consume_skb(). Mirror that in\nthe read_sock() path by recognizing an empty data record before\nthe actor runs, consuming it, and continuing.", "datePublished": "2026-08-15T05:55:40", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T18:55:18", "baseScore": 7.5, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0867b0f2513ebc1c475af9898c97f4772a68d964", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c6b440cf766a557b08d25f1b571b3d57d039686e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e8a4c9fc437b16aef38f86ce3275677e36924259", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ebc295ce343600c2d60c1e1e0c5d192080217457", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3be28e2c9cd0230cb51fd4967df095273afd3848"], "aliases": ["GHSA-744x-88r4-xj59", "CVE-2026-72330"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.62, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0002104e-468b-304d-ab3b-3a91a2173ebe", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "662fbcec32f4af6bdcf5b4006b792ebe9543d945 <3be28e2c9cd0230cb51fd4967df095273afd3848"}, {"id": "01d776ef-b239-36f1-838a-4802fbf3c5ae", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "662fbcec32f4af6bdcf5b4006b792ebe9543d945 <c6b440cf766a557b08d25f1b571b3d57d039686e"}, {"id": "1fe1d902-8c9e-396c-b6f1-75ac34a4f79f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.97"}, {"id": "2fc94d68-44df-3a66-828a-bd57ade6eea4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "662fbcec32f4af6bdcf5b4006b792ebe9543d945 <ebc295ce343600c2d60c1e1e0c5d192080217457"}, {"id": "31d5a258-e415-397b-9361-e5b5892f1782", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.5"}, {"id": "38c20703-7b1a-37dc-b16a-e9421e856261", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.40"}, {"id": "5fbab5cc-b9ff-33c0-a2b6-45e759424a57", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "7ec385da-75f3-3d4c-b848-b3a50a7ba69c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "662fbcec32f4af6bdcf5b4006b792ebe9543d945 <e8a4c9fc437b16aef38f86ce3275677e36924259"}, {"id": "8721aab0-7e8f-3440-9fd4-6ed8a05f48c0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "662fbcec32f4af6bdcf5b4006b792ebe9543d945 <0867b0f2513ebc1c475af9898c97f4772a68d964"}, {"id": "8e6929a3-a8fb-30e1-93e9-128598dbdf07", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.6"}, {"id": "a676808f-201c-3cbd-b125-15f75701bfec", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.145"}, {"id": "dc4a4ffb-35e4-35be-b831-22f15453ead2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "9f17e850-98d3-3a93-8c5d-400d5a939012", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}